lifeos-nix patch f4-c — Ship PULSE.toml with default-active egress/autonomous modules off

PROBLEM
  RedTeam EGRESS gap (a): the shipped PULSE.toml sets entries `enabled = true` that are
  default-ACTIVE (module loaded / job scheduled) rather than merely dispatch targets:
    - [voice]                      → VoiceServer module (cloud TTS path; hard-killed by f4-b,
                                     but the module still starts by default)
    - [telegram]                   → Telegram bot module
    - [[job]] life-morning-brief   → 7am job, output=voice

  LOS reconciliation (2026-08-07) surfaced three MORE default-active entries of the same
  class, which the original three-flip f4-c had missed:
    - [local_intelligence]         → module spawns skills/LocalIntelligence/Tools/Refresh.ts on
                                     a timer, which orchestrates EXTERNAL fetchers (patch.com
                                     news, US public records: crime/elections/legislation/…).
                                     A scheduled external-egress surface — same class as voice/
                                     telegram, NOT a mere dispatch target. Also US-only
                                     (Hometown = USPS state/county), zero value outside the US.
    - [[job]] airgradient-poll     → 5-min sensor poll; inert without AIRGRADIENT_TOKEN, but no
                                     sensor exists by default → default-off is cleaner hygiene.
    - [[job]] memory-consolidation → nightly 3am `type=claude` (Sonnet) autonomous pass over the
                                     last 20 sessions. Egress is to Anthropic (allowed by the
                                     invariant), but a privacy-minded base should not ship
                                     autonomous background AI + token spend on by default.

  Every OTHER external in the template is dispatch/target code that is env/cred-gated before
  the socket (telegram/email/ntfy/discord/twilio dispatchSingle skips without its env var;
  work/calendar/github config-gated) → inert with no creds, deliberately left enabled.

WHY THE FLIP SUFFICES (loader gates — pulse-unified.ts / pulse.ts)
  - module:  started only `if (config.X?.enabled !== false)` / `if (config.X?.enabled)` → false ⇒ never imported/started.
  - job:     scheduler does `if (!job.enabled) continue`                                → false ⇒ never scheduled/run.
  The flag is load-bearing; enabled=false makes the code path unreachable, not merely unused.

FIX
  Flip six shipped defaults to `enabled = false`: voice, telegram, life-morning-brief (original
  f4-c) + local_intelligence, airgradient-poll, memory-consolidation (LOS reconciliation
  2026-08-07). System-tier template; a user re-enables per entry via
  LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/PULSE.user.toml (merged by name, user-tier wins) — opt-in is one line,
  default inert. observability/hooks/performance/telos/da/cost-aggregation stay on (local-only).
  healthcheck stays on too, but its egress is user-configured, NOT Anthropic: ntfy notify
  (cred-gated) + probes of LIFEOS_PULSE_HEALTH_SITES if the principal sets them (exactly the K
  targets in egress-test's `{Anthropic} ∪ K`) — inert by default (empty env: no sites, no cred).

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One file, six one-line flips. Orthogonal to f4-a (lifeos.ts) and f4-b (voice/telegram/Doctor
  source). Complements f4-b: f4-b kills the ElevenLabs call in-code, f4-c stops modules/jobs
  from being default-active at all. ntfy/discord/twilio deliberately LEFT enabled (dispatch
  targets, inert without creds; egress-test proves ∅ external with empty env).

VERIFICATION
  Hunks via `diff -u` against extracted upstream (a4e8e74) PULSE.toml; `patch -p1 --dry-run`
  clean; built PULSE.toml shows the six `enabled = false`; egress-test.sh confirms ∅ external
  egress with no creds and voice/telegram OFF at boot.

